# Restore the real client IP from Cloudflare's CF-Connecting-IP header.
#
# All production traffic arrives via Cloudflare, so without this $remote_addr
# is a Cloudflare edge IP — and the edge a given client exits from rotates
# between requests. phpBB runs with ip_check=2 (compares the first two octets
# of the session's stored IP against the request IP), so a rotating edge IP
# invalidates the session on nearly every page load and bounces the user back
# to login. This also makes access logs, rate limiting, and bans meaningful.
#
# Loaded in every environment, not just production, so that it can never be
# a file that exists only in production, which is what it was when its
# absence invalidated every forum session at the last cutover.
#
# WHICH proxies are trusted to state the client's IP depends on who nginx's
# TCP peer is, and that is what LISTEN_MODE already describes:
#
#   listen-http, listen-tls   nginx is reached by Cloudflare directly (or by
#                             nobody but you, in dev): trust Cloudflare's
#                             ranges. In dev they are inert, since no request
#                             comes from them.
#   listen-proxied            nginx is reached only by the VPS's shared Caddy
#                             on the baja-edge network: trust that network
#                             alone. See listen-proxied-realip.conf.template.
#
# Hence one include per mode rather than one list here, selected the same way
# the listen blocks are.
#
# The 00- prefix is load-bearing: nginx includes conf.d/*.conf alphabetically
# inside the http block, and these directives must be parsed before the server
# blocks that inherit them.
include /etc/nginx/conf.d/snippets/${LISTEN_MODE}-realip.conf;
